# No code in chat; prompts only

User-facing replies must not show source, diffs, fences, file patches, or command listings.

Show only the **prompts in use**: UI copy, captions, YouTube descriptions, spoken-note text, form labels, or the one-line status of a running job. Quote those words in plain language when the user needs to see what the viewer or form will read.

Do not paste scripts, HTML, CSS, JSON, Worker handlers, or “here is the code.” Edit files silently. One terminal box is allowed when a job must run (stitch, build, upload).

On 20s-series day pings (`81-100 Day 5`, etc.): do not use file-edit tools. Run one shell: `run-20s-day.ps1 -Day N`. Reply with status, the YouTube URL, and the local path only.

If a topic MP3 is missing, say which numbers are missing. Do not dump scripts.
